#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "As step [30]."
msgstr "Comme l’étape [30]."

#: input/business-processes/GDHCN.TrustDomain.Join.bpmn:101
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Authorized WHO staff of the GDHCN Secretariat (Framework V, VI). ActorDefinition http://smart.who.int/trust/ActorDefinition/GDHCNSecretariat."
msgstr "Personnel autorisé de l’OMS au sein du Secrétariat du GDHCN (Cadre V, VI). ActorDefinition http://smart.who.int/trust/ActorDefinition/GDHCNSecretariat."

#: input/business-processes/GDHCN.TrustDomain.Join.bpmn:26
#. Diagram label
msgid "Business Owner Representative"
msgstr "Représentant du responsable métier"

#: input/business-processes/GDHCN.TrustDomain.Join.bpmn:46
#. Diagram label
msgid "Go live"
msgstr "Passer en production"

#: input/business-processes/GDHCN.TrustDomain.Join.bpmn:32
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Connects the Participant's systems to the Trust Network Gateway and runs the tests (Framework IX). ActorDefinition http://smart.who.int/trust/ActorDefinition/TechnicalRepresentative."
msgstr "Connecte les systèmes du Participant à la Passerelle du réseau de confiance et exécute les tests (Cadre IX). ActorDefinition http://smart.who.int/trust/ActorDefinition/TechnicalRepresentative."

#: input/business-processes/GDHCN.TrustDomain.Join.bpmn:41
#. Diagram label
msgid "Convey the Letter for it"
msgstr "Transmettre la Lettre correspondante"

#: input/business-processes/GDHCN.TrustDomain.Join.bpmn:37
#. Diagram label
msgid "Decided to join a further Trust Domain"
msgstr "Décision de rejoindre un Domaine de confiance supplémentaire"

#: input/business-processes/GDHCN.TrustDomain.Join.bpmn:42
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Framework IX: one Letter for each Trust Domain, on that Trust Domain's Annex form."
msgstr "Cadre IX : une Lettre pour chaque Domaine de confiance, sur le formulaire de l’Annexe de ce Domaine de confiance."

#: input/business-processes/GDHCN.TrustDomain.Join.bpmn:24
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Framework V.4 and IX."
msgstr "Cadre V.4 et IX."

